(
 '# GetDefaultMenubar'
 ''
 'This function returns the standard menubar definition:'
 ''
 '~~~'
 '      ⎕←⍪{addAfterEdit} GetDefaultMenubar debugFlag'
 '~~~'
 ''
 'With a `0` as left argument you get just the definition of the "Edit" menu:'
 ''
 '~~~'
 '      ⎕←⍪GUI.Input.GetDefaultMenubar 0'
 ' [&Edit]                         {edit}                                                                                                                                 '
 '  Cut=Ctrl+X        : <callback> {cut}          ;<description>'
 '  Copy=Ctrl+C       : <callback> {copy}         ;<description>'
 '  Paste=Ctrl+V      : <callback> {paste}        ;<description>'
 '~~~'
 ''
 'You can add your own stuff by passing it as left argument:'
 ''
 '~~~'
 '    q←''[Special]'' '' View : #.MyCallback {view} ; View in default Browser'''
 '    ⎕←⍪#.q Input.GetDefaultMenubar 1'
 ' [&Edit]                           {edit}                                                                                                                                 '
 '  Cut=Ctrl+X        : <callback>   {cut}           ;<description>'
 '  Copy=Ctrl+C       : <callback>   {copy}          ;<description>'
 '  Paste=Ctrl+V      : <callback>   {paste}         ;<description>'
 ' [Special] {special}                                                                                                                            '
 '  View              : #.MyCallback {view}          ;View in default Browser'
 ' [Developers]                      {developers}                                                                                                                       '
 '  Toggle magic grid : <callback>   {toggleMagic}   ;<description>'
 '  Edit callbacks... : <callback>   {editCallbacks} ;<description>'
 '  Browse "Input"    : <callback>   {editInput}     ;<description>'
 '~~~'
 ''
 'Notes:'
 ''
 '* We passed a `1` as argument and therefore got the definition of the "Developers" menu as well, offering additional features for developers.'
 '* Your own definition comes **after** the "Edit" menu but **before** the "Developers" menu if there is one.'
)
